---
app_name: MyApp
is_production: false
is_development: true
debug: false
---

> **Emitted frontmatter vs evaluated body:** runtime variables (`--vars`,
> `--set`, `--set-string`) override the evaluation scope — they control
> which `@if` branches fire and what `\{{variables}}` expand to. The emitted
> frontmatter in the compiled output is the template's own source YAML,
> verbatim; runtime overrides never alter it (spec §7.7). So the frontmatter
> below says `is_production: false` while the body renders production content
> because `vars.json` supplies `is_production: true` at evaluation time only.

# {{app_name}}

@if debug:
## Debug Mode Enabled

Verbose logging is ON. All queries will be traced.
@end

@if is_production:
## Production Checklist

- Ensure all secrets are rotated
- Verify CDN configuration
- Check rate limiting
@end

@if is_development:
## Development Notes

- Using local database
- Hot reload enabled
- Mock services active
@end
